rt Callable, Dict, Any\nfrom .tools import execute_sqlite_query, ExecuteQuerySchema\nfrom .memory import init_blackboard, record_event\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Simple model client stub \n<truncated 3047 bytes>\nhis stub with your local LLM (Ollama, llama.cpp, etc.) – the interface stays identical.  \n3. **Tool & Environment Layer** (`execute_sqlite_query`) runs a strict, validated SQLite query against `world_file.db`.  \n4. Each mutation is **logged** via `record_event`, giving a complete immutable audit trail (golden‑list‑ready).  \n\n### 4. ElevenLabs Integration (already in `ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh`)\n\n- The new `agent_speak.sh` first checks `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`.  \n- If present, it calls `elevenlabs_say.mjs`; otherwise it falls back to native `say` using the **Onyx** voice (if installed) or **Daniel**.  \n- You can now invoke speech like:\n\n```bash\nbash ops/scripts/agent_speak.sh jarvis \"All systems nominal on the USB workspace.\"\n```\n\n### 5. Production Guardrails (already enforced)\n\n| Guardrail | Implementation |\n|-----------|----------------|\n| **Hard Turn Limits** | `max_turns = 10` in `SimpleAgenticEnv` |\n| **Schema Validation** | Pydantic `ExecuteQuerySchema` – rejects malformed tool args |\n| **MARS Verification Gate** | `record_event` writes every action to the SQLite ledger (WAL) |\n| **Critic Peer Review** | The ledger can be inspected by a separate “critic” agent (e.g., `vance_critic.py`) that reads `event_log` and flags anomalies |\n| **Directory Guardrails** | `AGENTS.md` explicitly lists prohibited `barn/` directory |\n\n### 6. Next Steps You May Want\n\n- **Swap the dummy model** for a real local LLM (`ollama run llama3.2`, `llama.cpp`, etc.) – just implement a `generate(messages)` method that returns the same JSON shape.  \n- **Add a Critic agent** (`src/critic.py`) that reads `event_log` and validates groundedness scores before committing.  \n- **Expose a thin HTTP/WebSocket API